  "body": "These need to remain on any existing events so that hashes and signatures etc remain valid. But there is no reason for them hang around. As Rich wrote on MSC2176:\r\n\r\n> The following *event* keys are to be *removed* from the list of those to be\r\n> preserved by a redaction:\r\n> \r\n>  * `membership`\r\n>  * `prev_state`\r\n> \r\n> (Note this refers to the *event-level* `membership` property, rather than the\r\n> richvdh marked this conversation as resolved.\r\n> similarly-named sub-property under the `content` key.)\r\n> \r\n> Rationale: neither of the above properties have defined meanings any more in the Matrix\r\n> protocol, so there is no reason for them to be special-cased in this way.\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/issues/1091 and https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/2176\r\n\r\nI think we can remove `prev_state` from here\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/e0bb2681340752f2716f1f386139ca37c53f26cd/synapse/events/builder.py#L155-L165\r\n\r\nand here\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/bf0c3ca20a79136df962645d952ac75ce9d3615f/synapse/federation/federation_client.py#L800-L804\r\n",
